Tasks

1. Connect to your MongoDB server using the mongo shell and create a new database called insta_clone.

->  use insta_clone


2. Inside the insta_clone database, use the createUser command to add a user named 'storyAdmin' with the 'dbAdmin' role for managing Instagram Stories data.

->  db.createUser({
        user: "storyAdmin",
        pwd: "storyAdmin123",
        roles: [
            { role: "dbAdmin", db: "insta_clone" }
        ]
    })


3. Create a read-only user called 'feedViewer' in the insta_clone database who can only view (not modify) posts and comments collections.

->  db.createUser({
        user: "feedViewer",
        pwd: "feedViewer123",
        roles: [
            { role: "read", db: "insta_clone" }
        ]
    })  


4. Simulate authentication: Log in as 'feedViewer' and try to insert a new document into the posts collection. Note the error message and explain why it occurs.

->  mongosh -u feedViewer -p feedViewer123 --authenticationDatabase insta_clone


5. Use the db.getUsers() command to list all users in the insta_clone database and describe the roles assigned to each. Then, briefly explain in your own words the difference between 'read' and 'dbAdmin' roles.

->  db.getUsers()